# Project Overview

Rade Mate is a smart ride-sharing web application developed for college students. It allows students traveling on similar routes at similar times to share auto or cab rides, reducing travel expenses and making daily commuting more convenient.

---

# Problem Statement

College students often travel individually using autos and cabs, even when multiple students are heading to the same destination. This results in higher transportation costs and unnecessary vehicle usage.

Rade Mate solves this problem by connecting students with similar routes, allowing them to share rides and automatically split the fare.

---

# Objectives

- Reduce transportation costs.
- Enable easy ride sharing among students.
- Match students traveling on similar routes.
- Automatically calculate fare sharing.
- Provide a simple and responsive user experience.

---

# Tech Stack

### Frontend
- React.js (Vite)
- Tailwind CSS
- React Router
- Axios

### Backend
- FastAPI (Python)
- Uvicorn
- Pydantic

### Data Storage
- In-memory Python lists and dictionaries (No Database)

